  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Evening Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    15 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good evening Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,176.50/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,167.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NORTHWEST</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MAINLAND</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SOBAZ</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,170.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,175.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,661.62/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,608.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Prices Weekly Review: 10th–14th August 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s downstream petroleum market recorded mixed depot price movements between Monday, August 10 and Friday, August 14, 2026. While some depots raised their prices, others reduced their rates or held steady. AGO recorded the strongest price movements during the week, particularly in Lagos and Warri, while PMS prices generally posted smaller adjustments.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-prices-weekly-review-10th14th-august-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NUPRC Unveils Crude Swap Plan to Boost Supply, Cut Refinery Costs\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian Upstream Petroleum Regulatory Commission is working on a domestic crude oil and gas swap arrangement. The proposal is aimed at reducing supply costs and improving feedstock availability for local refineries. The proposed framework is expected to strengthen compliance with the Domestic Crude Supply Obligation.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nuprc-unveils-crude-swap-plan-to-boost-supply-cut-refinery-costs\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    PETROAN Backs Tinubu’s Refinery Push, Warns NNPCL Against Another Costly Failure\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s latest push to revive its state-owned refineries must move beyond rehabilitation promises and commissioning ceremonies, the Petroleum Products Retail Outlets Owners Association of Nigeria has warned. PETROAN backed President Bola Tinubu's renewed commitment to restoring the Port Harcourt and Warri refineries, but said the initiative will only succeed if NNPC Ltd ties the proposed partnership to firm deadlines.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/petroan-backs-tinubus-refinery-push-warns-nnpcl-against-another-costly-failure\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Calabar Petrol Price War Intensifies as Depot Prices Near Lagos Levels\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Petrol prices in Calabar are coming under increasing pressure as competing marketers push depot prices lower. This has narrowed the gap with Lagos, Nigeria’s traditional low-price hub for refined petroleum products.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/calabar-petrol-price-war-intensifies-as-depot-prices-near-lagos-levels\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Tinubu Vows to Revive Nigeria's Refineries, Promises Structural Reset\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    President Bola Tinubu has assured that Nigeria's refineries will be revived and repositioned to become profitable. The President gave the assurance on Thursday when he received the newly elected national executive of the Nigerian Union of Petroleum and Natural Gas Workers (NUPENG) He added that a refinery producing flame and smoke does not necessarily mean it is functional.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/tinubu-vows-to-revive-nigerias-refineries-promises-structural-reset\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
